104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (To maintain the business's core offerings, the Manage Services Page offers a suite of interactive tools for inventory oversight. This interface allows the administrator to dynamically expand the service catalog via the "Add Service" feature, which uses programmatic prompts to capture new service details and render them as interactive cards. Furthermore, the system supports immediate modifications through an "Edit" function and permanent removal via a "Delete" button. This ensures that the user interface is always a direct reflection of the underlying data array, providing a "what-you-see-is-what-you-have" management experience.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 504 0 R
/E (Dynamic Order Management and Data Processing)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (The Manage Orders Page represents the most technologically advanced component of the system, featuring a highly functional dynamic data table. Designed to manage complex records efficiently, it includes a "New Booking" feature for manual administrative entries. To optimize operational speed, this feature is programmed to automatically assign an "Accepted" status to these entries. The page is further enhanced with sorting algorithms, allowing the manager to organize data by "Highest Amount" or "Newest Date." To maintain a clean and professional UI, a custom "Pagination" logic was implemented, limiting the display to four records per page and utilizing state variables to re-render the table dynamically as the user navigates.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
